 "known_gaps": [
  "Dispatch_Date is stored in both dispatch and turnaround_time in the source CSVs; the canonical model owns it once (on dispatch).",
  "tracking.last_known_location mixes hub codes (Hub_323) and city names in one column.",
  "turnaround_time.total_tat_hours takes only about 22 distinct values: bucketed, not raw.",
  "There are no dimension tables for drivers, warehouses or carriers.",
  "Plants use different physical table names (dispatch vs ycw_dispatch vs vgu_dispatch); ir/adapters.py normalizes this once, at IR level.",
  "Plants run different engines (SQLite, DuckDB, PostgreSQL-capable); timestamps are TEXT in SQLite but TIMESTAMP in DuckDB and PostgreSQL. Dialect handling: docs/dialects.md.",
  "Each plant holds a disjoint third of the invoices (invoice sequence number mod 3), so plant-level totals only make sense summed across plants."
 ],
